From 8ce54dca067e568c937691e6852b19203b2f3b2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 02:43:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Allow editing questions in the pre-publish review

In the "Review questions" panel the admin can now edit each question's
text, context, options (add/remove) and correct answer; matching tasks can
change the correct bank letter. Edits are kept client-side, validated in the
UI (save is disabled while an edit is invalid) and sent with mode=save as
`edits`. The server re-validates with the parser's limits and applies them
atomically (any error rejects all edits) before saving, via the new
placementTestEdits.js. The audit log records editedQuestions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M5ovApmXiMwLLizrjsPGkJ
